# Conventional Commits

All commit messages must follow [Conventional Commits 1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/).

## Format

```
<type>(optional scope): <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

## Allowed types

| Type | When to use |
|------|-------------|
| `feat` | New feature |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `chore` | Maintenance, deps, tooling |
| `refactor` | Code change without feature or fix |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `style` | Formatting, no logic change |
| `test` | Adding or fixing tests |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `build` | Build system changes |
| `ci` | CI/CD config changes |
| `revert` | Reverting a commit |

## Rules

- Header max length: **150 characters**
- Description: lowercase, no period at the end
- Use imperative mood: "add", not "added" or "adds"

## Examples

```
# ✅ GOOD
feat(auth): add sign in with Apple
fix(api): handle 401 response on token refresh
chore: add husky and lint-staged
refactor(ui): extract Button into shared component

# ❌ BAD
Added new screen        ← no type
feat: Added new screen. ← past tense + period
FEAT: new screen        ← uppercase type
```
